    "body": "## Summary\n- close requester exact-location and exact-route API access after `DONE` or `CANCELLED`\n- preserve requester access while an own job is still `OPEN`\n- preserve requester/assigned-worker access for `IN_PROGRESS`, `COMPLETION_REQUESTED`, and `DISPUTED`\n- add focused lifecycle authorization tests\n- document the boundary and explicitly separate API access minimization from future persisted-location retention/purge policy\n\n## Why\nExact coordinates and private route/address data are execution data. The assigned worker was already denied after completion, but the requester could continue reading exact historical location indefinitely because requester ownership bypassed lifecycle checks. This closes that asymmetric privacy gap without deleting evidence from money-sensitive terminal transactions.\n\n## Validation\nRequired before merge: exact-head API/Maven verification, frontend tests/audit/lint/build, production Compose contract, and runtime/container smokes. Do not merge on pending/failing checks.",
